      "problem": "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle t^6,\\, t^5\\rangle,$ Calculate $\\mathbf r''(t).$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t) = t^6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =6{t}^{5} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =30{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) = t^5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =5{t}^{4} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =20{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨30{t}^{4},\\,20{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =10⟨3{t}^{4},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
